<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikolai Avksentiev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikolai Avksentiev was a Russian Socialist Revolutionary politician who served as interior minister in the Provisional Government in 1917. In September 1918 he became chairman of the five-member Directory of the All-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-provisional-government">Russian Provisional Government</a> formed at Ufa, which moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omsk">Omsk</a>. Officers overthrew it in November 1918 in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kolchak">Admiral Kolchak</a>, and Avksentiev was expelled abroad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikolai-avksentiev.jpg" alt="Nikolai Avksentiev" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Chevalier · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicolas_Avksentieff_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
